Honest answer: **not critical right now**. Ship what you have first.

Here's why — EfficientNet-B0 would give you better accuracy on the harder cases (blurry photos, varied scenes), but the gains come from the architecture having more capacity, not from magic. Your current retrain with the category-balanced dataset is almost certainly already a meaningful improvement over the 3-class CIFAKE-only model. The dataset quality improvement matters more than the architecture choice at this stage.

The question to ask is: does your current model fail on real-world test images? Upload a few selfies and landscape photos after deployment. If accuracy looks good, you're done. If you're still seeing obvious mistakes, then retrain with EfficientNet-B0.

